  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Dinitrogen and dioxygen are the main constituents of air. These gases do not react with each other at a normal temperature. At high altitudes when lightning strikes, they combine to form oxides of nitrogen.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>NO reacts instantly with oxygen to give NO<sub>2</sub></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>NO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Rate of production of NO<sub>2</sub> is faster when nitric oxide reacts with ozone in the stratosphere</p><p>The irritant red haze in the traffic and congested places is due to oxides of nitrogen. Higher concentrations of NO<sub>2</sub> damage the leaves of plants and retard the rate of photosynthesis. It is toxic to living tissues also</p></blockquote>",
